1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,192
Part 1: You will hear a
man phoning a community

2
00:00:03,216 --> 00:00:06,012
center to book a
room for a family party.

3
00:00:06,499 --> 00:00:09,940
First, you have some time
to look at questions 1 to 6.

4
00:00:40,039 --> 00:00:43,440
Yes, it's Daniel Cartwell.

5
00:00:44,639 --> 00:00:46,560
Daniel... Cartwright, was that?

6
00:00:47,180 --> 00:00:55,180
Everyone says that.
No, it's Cartwell. C-A-R-T-W-E-L-L.

7
00:00:55,529 --> 00:01:01,340
C-A-R-T-W-E-L-L.

8
00:01:01,390 --> 00:01:05,420
Got it. Thank you.
And what sort of date were you thinking of?

9
00:01:05,469 --> 00:01:09,167
Well, her actual birthday is
Wednesday the 10th of May,

10
00:01:09,191 --> 00:01:12,632
but obviously a weekday
is no good for most people,

11
00:01:12,719 --> 00:01:16,620
so we were looking at the
Saturday after that. The 13th.

12
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:20,534
Ah, I'm afraid the 13th has
gone. We've got a wedding

13
00:01:20,558 --> 00:01:24,632
reception in all day. How
about the following Saturday?

14
00:01:24,769 --> 00:01:27,100
So, that'd be the 20th?

15
00:01:27,149 --> 00:01:30,620
That's right.
The 20th is completely free at the moment.

16
00:01:30,719 --> 00:01:33,754
Then let's go for that. My
sister did say she couldn't

17
00:01:33,778 --> 00:01:36,712
make the 13th anyway,
so it's probably for the best.

18
00:01:36,713 --> 00:01:41,660
Lovely. I'll pencil you in. And roughly,
how many guests are you expecting?

19
00:01:41,709 --> 00:01:45,208
That's the tricky bit. We
sent out 60 invitations,

20
00:01:45,232 --> 00:01:48,392
but quite a few people
are bringing partners,

21
00:01:48,479 --> 00:01:51,469
and Mum keeps adding
cousins I've never heard of.

22
00:01:51,493 --> 00:01:54,312
So realistically, we're
planning for about 85.

23
00:01:55,109 --> 00:01:58,629
85. Right, that does
narrow things down.

24
00:01:58,653 --> 00:02:04,260
Our willow room is lovely, but
it only takes 45, so that's out.

25
00:02:04,261 --> 00:02:06,860
The main hall holds 200…

26
00:02:07,209 --> 00:02:09,340
That sounds a bit enormous for us.

27
00:02:09,341 --> 00:02:12,972
It can feel rather empty
with a smaller group, yes.

28
00:02:12,996 --> 00:02:16,712
So I'd suggest the orchard
room. It takes up to 100,

29
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:19,340
and it opens straight onto
the garden, which is nice in May.

30
00:02:19,341 --> 00:02:23,420
Oh, that sounds perfect.
Mum's a keen gardener.

31
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:28,940
Now, the price. On a Saturday,
the standard rate is £45 an hour.

32
00:02:28,941 --> 00:02:30,780
Ah, right.

33
00:02:30,880 --> 00:02:34,634
No, hang on. Sorry. That's
the main hall. I was looking

34
00:02:34,658 --> 00:02:38,152
at the wrong line. The
orchard room is £38 an hour.

35
00:02:38,290 --> 00:02:41,572
38? That's better than I
expected. Is there a discount

36
00:02:41,596 --> 00:02:44,952
for people who live locally?
Someone told me there was.

37
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:49,020
There used to be, but the trustees
stopped it last year, I'm afraid.

38
00:02:49,070 --> 00:02:53,580
Never mind. And what time could we get in?
We'd want to put decorations up.

39
00:02:53,730 --> 00:02:57,980
The room's free from midday, so
you can come in any time after that,

40
00:02:58,080 --> 00:03:01,580
but the time you spend decorating
does count towards the hire.

41
00:03:02,610 --> 00:03:06,060
Then we'll be quick about it.
Probably three o'clock until eleven.

42
00:03:06,864 --> 00:03:10,860
Three till eleven.
Now, as for what's included…

43
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:14,229
Tables and chairs, of
course, and we can lend

44
00:03:14,253 --> 00:03:16,632
you white tablecloths
at no extra charge.

45
00:03:17,355 --> 00:03:21,260
There's a fully equipped kitchen
with plates and cutlery for a hundred.

46
00:03:21,261 --> 00:03:22,261
And glasses?

47
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:28,860
We had a set of glasses, but so many got
broken that we don't supply them anymore.

48
00:03:28,910 --> 00:03:32,460
So you'd have to bring your
own glasses or hire some.

49
00:03:32,461 --> 00:03:35,660
Right. I'll ask the caterers.
They might have some.

50
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:38,418
Before you hear the rest
of the conversation, you

51
00:03:38,442 --> 00:03:41,112
have some time to look
at questions seven to ten.

52
00:04:01,810 --> 00:04:04,410
Now, there are a few other things
I should mention. Parking first.

53
00:04:11,210 --> 00:04:16,459
Yes, that'll matter.
A lot of Mum's friends drive.

54
00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:24,978
Well, the car park has 40 spaces and it doesn't
shut at night, so nobody gets locked in. People

55
00:04:25,002 --> 00:04:28,872
used to need a permit to park there, but we
got rid of that system a couple of years ago.

56
00:04:28,873 --> 00:04:30,060
Great.

57
00:04:33,260 --> 00:04:37,248
The only thing is, there's a yoga class in the
studio on Saturday evenings, and they normally take

58
00:04:37,272 --> 00:04:41,272
about a dozen of those spaces until half past
seven, so your first guests might struggle a little.

59
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:44,720
Okay. I'll tell people
not to come too early.

60
00:04:44,744 --> 00:04:48,872
Now, music. My cousin's
band is playing. Is that alright?

61
00:04:48,960 --> 00:04:52,053
Of course. Our license runs
until midnight on Saturdays.

62
00:04:52,077 --> 00:04:55,667
It's only on weekday evenings
that things have to stop at eleven.

63
00:04:55,668 --> 00:04:58,300
And would they have to
use your sound system?

64
00:04:58,350 --> 00:05:01,420
No, they don't need to.
Most bands prefer their own.

65
00:05:02,140 --> 00:05:06,128
What we do ask, though, is that you put a
short note through the doors of the houses

66
00:05:06,152 --> 00:05:10,152
on Mill Lane, at least a week before the
party, so they know there'll be some noise.

67
00:05:10,290 --> 00:05:12,940
We've had complaints in the
past when people weren't warned.

68
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:17,900
That's fair enough. I can do that.
And will you be doing the food yourselves?

69
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:22,495
That's been a long family debate.
My aunt offered to cook everything,

70
00:05:22,519 --> 00:05:26,632
but she's 73 herself and we didn't
want her stuck in a kitchen all night.

71
00:05:26,670 --> 00:05:29,513
Then someone suggested
everybody bringing a dish, but Mum

72
00:05:29,537 --> 00:05:32,392
said that would be like asking
her guests to pay to come.

73
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:34,620
I can see her point.

74
00:05:34,720 --> 00:05:37,970
So, in the end, we've gone
for a local firm, Hollis Catering.

75
00:05:37,994 --> 00:05:42,152
They'll bring hot dishes already cooked
and just keep them warm in your ovens.

76
00:05:42,190 --> 00:05:46,940
That's no problem at all.
Finally, there's a deposit of £100 to

77
00:05:46,941 --> 00:05:51,100
secure the date, and you get that
back as long as the room's left tidy.

78
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:53,980
Can I pay that now? I've got my card here.

79
00:05:54,430 --> 00:05:57,795
Normally, yes, but our card
machine's being replaced

80
00:05:57,819 --> 00:06:00,872
this week, so I can't
take cards at the moment.

81
00:06:01,510 --> 00:06:04,880
And we don't accept bank
transfers anymore. Our treasurer

82
00:06:04,904 --> 00:06:07,752
found it too hard to match
payments to bookings.

83
00:06:07,753 --> 00:06:12,135
So… So, you'd need to
drop it into the office here,

84
00:06:12,159 --> 00:06:15,912
cash or a cheque. We're
open 9 till 5 on weekdays.

85
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:19,580
I'm driving past on Thursday
anyway, so I'll call in then.

86
00:06:19,890 --> 00:06:23,564
Perfect. I'll hold the room
until Friday, and once the

87
00:06:23,588 --> 00:06:27,752
deposit's in, it's confirmed.
And happy birthday to your mum!

88
00:06:27,790 --> 00:06:30,780
Thanks. I'll pass that on. Bye now!

89
00:06:32,030 --> 00:06:37,900
That is the end of Part 1. You now have
one minute to check your answers to Part 1.

