105
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:41,192
Part 2. You will hear a
volunteer coordinator

106
00:07:41,216 --> 00:07:44,220
talking to a group of
new volunteers about a

107
00:07:44,221 --> 00:07:51,260
City Farm's Open Day. First, you have
some time to look at questions 11 to 15.

108
00:08:06,130 --> 00:08:08,050
You have some time to
look at questions 11 to 15.

109
00:08:20,590 --> 00:08:25,020
Right. Good morning, everyone, and
thank you so much for coming along.

110
00:08:25,021 --> 00:08:27,482
I'm Megan. I coordinate
the volunteers here

111
00:08:27,506 --> 00:08:30,147
at Brickfield City Farm,
and I'll be your main

112
00:08:30,148 --> 00:08:34,780
point of contact on Saturday. I know
one or two of you have helped out before,

113
00:08:34,929 --> 00:08:38,380
but most of you are new, so I'll go
through everything from the beginning.

114
00:08:39,069 --> 00:08:43,900
Now, you may have heard that this is our
20th year, and yes, there will be a cake.

115
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:50,060
A very large one. But the anniversary isn't
really why we're holding the Open Day.

116
00:08:50,109 --> 00:08:51,635
Nor is it mainly about money.

117
00:08:51,659 --> 00:08:54,867
We'll have collection buckets,
of course, but the new roof

118
00:08:54,868 --> 00:08:58,140
for the goat barn has already
been paid for by a council grant.

119
00:08:58,929 --> 00:09:01,832
The honest truth is that
we're seriously short of

120
00:09:01,856 --> 00:09:04,707
regular helpers, especially
on weekday mornings,

121
00:09:04,708 --> 00:09:08,940
and an Open Day is far and away the
best way we've found of signing people up.

122
00:09:09,425 --> 00:09:13,100
So, if anyone shows an interest,
please send them to the Green Gazebo.

123
00:09:13,799 --> 00:09:16,237
A few things are
different from last year.

124
00:09:16,261 --> 00:09:19,512
Last time, we charged visitors
three pounds at the gate,

125
00:09:19,599 --> 00:09:22,532
which caused long queues
and, frankly, put some

126
00:09:22,556 --> 00:09:25,752
local families off. This
year, thanks to a sponsor,

127
00:09:25,864 --> 00:09:28,442
there won't be any charge
at all. Some people have

128
00:09:28,466 --> 00:09:31,424
rung up asking whether they
need to book a place online.

129
00:09:31,425 --> 00:09:33,819
They don't. They
can just turn up.

130
00:09:33,843 --> 00:09:37,752
And the hours are exactly
the same as before, 10 until 4.

131
00:09:38,430 --> 00:09:41,154
Right, the animals. The
rabbits are always the

132
00:09:41,178 --> 00:09:44,152
most popular, with the
guinea pigs a close second.

133
00:09:44,769 --> 00:09:47,282
Children can feed them.
We sell little bags of

134
00:09:47,306 --> 00:09:49,832
feed for 50 pence, and
that's absolutely fine.

135
00:09:50,419 --> 00:09:53,774
What we don't allow is children
walking around holding them.

136
00:09:53,798 --> 00:09:58,416
Rabbits wriggle, and if they're dropped,
they can be badly hurt. So, the rule is

137
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:01,112
that the child sits
down on the bench first,

138
00:10:01,150 --> 00:10:04,087
and then you place the
rabbit on a towel on their lap.

139
00:10:04,111 --> 00:10:06,467
Last year, we put the
rabbits back in their

140
00:10:06,468 --> 00:10:08,995
hutches at lunchtime
to give them a rest, but in

141
00:10:09,019 --> 00:10:11,672
fact, they coped perfectly
well, so they'll be out

142
00:10:11,673 --> 00:10:15,128
all day this time. People
often ask me what I worry

143
00:10:15,152 --> 00:10:18,632
about most on the day.
Parking always looks chaotic

144
00:10:18,744 --> 00:10:21,174
from the gate, but it
does sort itself out, because

145
00:10:21,198 --> 00:10:23,592
the school next door lets
us use their playground.

146
00:10:24,139 --> 00:10:26,821
And the queue for the
cafe can get long, but people

147
00:10:26,845 --> 00:10:29,592
are usually very patient
when there's cake involved.

148
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:34,431
No, what really keeps me
awake is the lost children's point.

149
00:10:34,455 --> 00:10:37,500
Last year, we had 11
children separated from

150
00:10:37,501 --> 00:10:40,907
their parents in a single
afternoon, and one little

151
00:10:40,931 --> 00:10:44,540
boy was missing for nearly
40 minutes. So whoever's on

152
00:10:44,541 --> 00:10:48,161
that point needs to stay
there, and not wander off

153
00:10:48,185 --> 00:10:51,672
to help elsewhere. And
the weather. If it rains,

154
00:10:51,834 --> 00:10:54,253
the tractor rides will
still run, because the

155
00:10:54,277 --> 00:10:57,027
trailer's covered. We used
to move the craft tables

156
00:10:57,028 --> 00:10:59,629
into the big barn when
it rained, but the noise

157
00:10:59,653 --> 00:11:03,097
upset the animals, so now they
go into the classroom instead.

158
00:11:03,098 --> 00:11:05,940
The only activity
we'll actually call off

159
00:11:05,964 --> 00:11:09,512
is the pony rides. The
ground gets far too slippery.

160
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:14,261
Before you hear the
rest of the talk, you

161
00:11:14,285 --> 00:11:18,472
have some time to look
at questions 16 to 20.

162
00:11:45,969 --> 00:11:48,457
Okay, if you look at the
plan I've given you, I'll

163
00:11:48,481 --> 00:11:51,032
show you where everything's
going to be on the day.

164
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:54,574
We're standing at the
main entrance, at the bottom

165
00:11:54,598 --> 00:11:58,231
of the plan, facing into the
farm, so north is straight ahead.

166
00:11:58,232 --> 00:12:00,464
The main path
runs from here up to

167
00:12:00,488 --> 00:12:03,820
the duck pond in the
middle. It then splits and goes

168
00:12:03,821 --> 00:12:08,140
round both sides of the pond, and the
two halves join up again on the far side.

169
00:12:08,889 --> 00:12:11,850
First aid. In previous
years, the first aid post

170
00:12:11,874 --> 00:12:15,032
was right beside the
cafe, which is just inside the

171
00:12:15,033 --> 00:12:18,296
gate on your left. But it
got far too crowded there,

172
00:12:18,320 --> 00:12:21,672
so this year it's moving
further up on the same side,

173
00:12:21,709 --> 00:12:24,983
right against the west fence,
just south of the big barn.

174
00:12:25,007 --> 00:12:27,031
So it isn't on the
main path at all.

175
00:12:27,032 --> 00:12:31,208
It's over by the fence. Now,
the lost children's point, and

176
00:12:31,232 --> 00:12:34,780
please do remember
where this is. Lots of parents

177
00:12:34,781 --> 00:12:37,886
assume it'll be at the
entrance, and we'll put a sign

178
00:12:37,910 --> 00:12:40,792
up here, but the point
itself is beyond the pond,

179
00:12:40,879 --> 00:12:43,796
at the place where the
two paths meet again.

180
00:12:43,820 --> 00:12:47,272
So that's on the north
side of the pond. Pony rides.

181
00:12:47,359 --> 00:12:49,486
You'd expect them to
be in the paddock, but the

182
00:12:49,510 --> 00:12:52,379
paddock's being used for the
sheep shearing display this year.

183
00:12:52,380 --> 00:12:54,423
So the ponies
will be in the small

184
00:12:54,447 --> 00:12:57,352
field in the bottom
right-hand corner of the site,

185
00:12:57,439 --> 00:13:00,418
the southeast corner, to
your right as you come in.

186
00:13:00,442 --> 00:13:03,432
The plant sale is new
this year. It'll be along the

187
00:13:03,433 --> 00:13:06,456
north fence at the very
top of the plan, halfway

188
00:13:06,480 --> 00:13:08,865
between the big
barn and the orchard.

189
00:13:08,903 --> 00:13:12,392
It won't be inside the orchard
itself, I'm afraid, because

190
00:13:12,416 --> 00:13:14,682
the trees are being
pruned that week.

191
00:13:14,683 --> 00:13:17,238
And finally, the
cheese-making demonstration.

192
00:13:17,262 --> 00:13:20,712
Originally, we'd planned to
have it in the barn, by the door,

193
00:13:20,899 --> 00:13:23,110
but there just isn't
enough light in there.

194
00:13:23,134 --> 00:13:25,512
So it'll be over on the
east side of the site,

195
00:13:25,649 --> 00:13:28,081
between the orchard
and the paddock, right up

196
00:13:28,105 --> 00:13:31,201
against the east fence.
Right. That's everything for me.

197
00:13:31,202 --> 00:13:34,268
Grab a coffee, and I'll
come round and give

198
00:13:34,292 --> 00:13:37,592
you your t-shirts. That
is the end of part two.

